<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">László Rajk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">László Rajk was a Hungarian communist who served as minister of the interior from 1946 to 1948 and then as foreign minister. In 1949 he was arrested, accused of spying for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito">Tito</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> and the West, and condemned in a show trial organised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matyas-rakosi">Mátyás Rákosi</a>; he was executed in October 1949. His reburial in October 1956 helped spark the Hungarian Revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laszlo-rajk.jpg" alt="László Rajk" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kommunizmuskutató Intézet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajk_Laszlo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Mátyás Rákosi, leader of the Hungarian Working People's Party, ruled as a Stalinist dictator, with show trials such as that of <b>László Rajk</b> and a feared secret police, the ÁVH.</blockquote><a href="/state/hungarian-peoples-republic">Hungarian People's Republic</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Odorheiu Secuiesc, in what is now <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=46.31,25.3&amp;year=1935" aria-label="Odorheiu Secuiesc on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5147 534 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of László Rajk"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5597 804h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5597 804h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=46.31,25.3&amp;year=1935">What was here in 1935? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
